.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH taurctl-pkg 1  "taurctl-pkg " 
.SH NAME
taurctl\-pkg \- Manage package ownership
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtaurctl pkg\fR [\fB\-\-server\fR] [\fB\-\-config\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-password\-stdin\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage package ownership
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-server\fR \fI<SERVER>\fR
Server URL (overrides TAUR_SERVER and the config file)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_SERVER\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-config\-dir\fR \fI<CONFIG_DIR>\fR
Config directory (default: $TAURCTL_CONFIG_DIR, else $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/taurctl)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print raw JSON
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Don\*(Aqt ask for confirmation
.TP
\fB\-\-password\-stdin\fR
Read the password from the first line of stdin instead of prompting
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
taurctl\-pkg\-list(1)
Package bases you can manage
.TP
taurctl\-pkg\-adopt(1)
Adopt an orphaned package base
.TP
taurctl\-pkg\-disown(1)
Give up maintainership (package becomes orphaned)
.TP
taurctl\-pkg\-vote(1)
Vote for a package base
.TP
taurctl\-pkg\-unvote(1)
Remove your vote
.TP
taurctl\-pkg\-flag(1)
Flag a package base out\-of\-date
.TP
taurctl\-pkg\-unflag(1)
Remove the out\-of\-date flag (maintainers or the flagger)
.TP
taurctl\-pkg\-comments(1)
Show comments on a package base
.TP
taurctl\-pkg\-comment(1)
Comment on a package base
.TP
taurctl\-pkg\-comaintainers(1)
Set the co\-maintainers of a package base (replaces the list; none clears it)
.TP
taurctl\-pkg\-transfer(1)
Transfer a package base to an organization or a user
.TP
taurctl\-pkg\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
